Description – This api takes a food item name (in the variable named regex) and gives details about it like ingredients, nutritional values, allergens, etc. This  is the base api for recipe.
Method - POST
Parameters - A food item name
AI request - 
{
    "api1": {
        "url": "https://dcponazure-entity-api03.azurewebsites.net/api/v1/entities/PRODUCT/query/",
        "payLoad": {
            "pageNumber": 0,
            "itemsPerPage": 10,
            "fields": [
                {
                    "name": "name",
                    "match": {
                        "regex": "muffin bUrGeR",
                        "ignoreCase": true
                    }
                }
            ]
        }
    }
}	

Description - This api takes a food item id (entityId) in the url and gives its recipe. This API exclusively serves recipe details and does not include other information such as ingredients, nutritional values, or allergens. To get the entityId, hit this api and get the id from its response https://dcponazure-entity-api03.azurewebsites.net/api/v1/entities/PRODUCT/query/            
Method - POST
Parameters – A food item id
AI request -
{
    "api2": {
        "url": "https://dcponazure-entity-api03.azurewebsites.net/api/v1/entities/PRODUCT/{entityId}/features/query/",
        "payLoad": {
            "typeCodes": [
                "RECIPE"
            ]
        }
    }
}

Description – This api takes an ingredient name (in the variable named regex) and gives various details about it like unit of measurement, storage, etc.
Method – POST
Parameters – An ingredient name
AI request -
{
    "api3": {
        "url": "https://dcponazure-entity-api03.azurewebsites.net/api/v1/entities/INGREDIENT/query/",
        "payLoad": {
  "pageNumber": 0,
  "itemsPerPage": 10,
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "name",
      "match": {
        "regex": "corn",
        "ignoreCase": true
      }
    }
  ]
        }
    }
}

Description – This api takes a food item id (entityId) in the url and gives its ingredients and details about those ingredients. To get the entityId, hit this api and get the id from its response https://dcponazure-entity-api03.azurewebsites.net/api/v1/entities/PRODUCT/query/
Method – POST
Parameters – A food item id
AI request -
{
    "api4": {
        "url": "https://dcponazure-entity-api03.azurewebsites.net/api/v1/entities/PRODUCT/{entityId}/associations/query/",
        "payLoad": {
{
  "typeCodes": [
    "PRODUCT_INGREDIENT"
  ],
  "retrieveOtherEntities": true
}

        }
    }
}

Description - This api takes email domain (in the variable named regex) and gender value (in the variable named value). For gender value capital M stands for Male and capital F for Female. Then it gives details about all the customers with email of same domain and given gender.
Method – POST
Parameters – Email domain and Gender
AI request -
{
    "api5": {
        "url": "https://dcponazure-entity-api03.azurewebsites.net/api/v1/entities/CUSTOMER/query/",
        "payLoad": {
{
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "email",
      "match": {
        "regex": "capgemini.com",
     "ignoreCase": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "gender",
      "match": {
        "value": "M"
      }
    }  
  ]
}
        }
    }
}


